WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.580
One hillside of grass grows lush while another stays sparse.

2
00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:10.840
Why? Two real sites differ in soil, slope, rain, and history all at once.

3
00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:15.620
Watching nature alone cannot separate those tangled factors.

4
00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:22.520
A field manipulation experiment tests cause by changing one factor inside one place.

5
00:00:25.583 --> 00:00:30.863
Inside that one grassland, divide the slope into matched blocks with similar soil.

6
00:00:32.163 --> 00:00:35.003
Within each block, mark equal plots and flip a coin.

7
00:00:36.303 --> 00:00:40.063
Some plots receive the treatment; untouched plots serve as controls.

8
00:00:41.603 --> 00:00:43.623
Choosing by eye could pick the healthiest spots.

9
00:00:45.323 --> 00:00:49.983
Random assignment removes that bias and balances hidden differences on average.

10
00:00:51.117 --> 00:00:54.257
Now change one factor while keeping plot area alike.

11
00:00:55.557 --> 00:00:59.217
You can remove a species, or add a resource like water or light.

12
00:01:00.337 --> 00:01:05.037
Or build an exclosure: a cage or shelter that keeps one influence out.

13
00:01:06.217 --> 00:01:11.457
To test cause in nature, change one factor at random while matched controls hold

14
00:01:11.457 --> 00:01:12.517
everything else alike.

15
00:01:13.617 --> 00:01:17.317
Picture rain-out shelters built over those grassland plots.

16
00:01:18.717 --> 00:01:20.037
Roofs block natural rain.

17
00:01:21.337 --> 00:01:26.277
Irrigation then returns the same total, either in the natural pattern or as fewer,

18
00:01:26.697 --> 00:01:31.197
larger storms. Yet each roof stays over the grass all season.

19
00:01:32.497 --> 00:01:36.697
What side effect could mislead you, and what extra control plot checks for it?

20
00:01:42.117 --> 00:01:45.577
A shelter can cast shade and warm the air beneath it.

21
00:01:46.777 --> 00:01:51.617
So experimenters add unsheltered plots to check whether the roof itself changed

22
00:01:51.617 --> 00:01:57.537
plant growth. They also log soil moisture to confirm the treatment made moisture

23
00:01:57.537 --> 00:02:03.517
more variable. Cage exclosures need a similar check: report how well the mesh

24
00:02:03.517 --> 00:02:05.037
actually kept predators out.

25
00:02:06.050 --> 00:02:08.250
Even careful controls have limits.

26
00:02:09.510 --> 00:02:14.270
With only one treated block, chance differences can mimic a real effect, so

27
00:02:14.270 --> 00:02:15.770
treatments must be replicated.

28
00:02:17.190 --> 00:02:21.890
One unusual year of weather can also dominate, so plots are tracked for several

29
00:02:21.890 --> 00:02:28.910
years. And a field result applies to that site first; another grassland or shore can

30
00:02:28.910 --> 00:02:29.910
respond differently.

31
00:02:30.983 --> 00:02:33.403
These designs unlocked real causes.

32
00:02:34.763 --> 00:02:40.263
In 2002, Knapp and colleagues ran those shelters for four years in a grassland with

33
00:02:40.263 --> 00:02:46.823
moderate rain. Fewer, larger events raised soil-moisture variability, lowered plant

34
00:02:46.823 --> 00:02:49.263
growth, and raised species diversity.

35
00:02:50.763 --> 00:02:54.103
Fertilized experimental grassland communities lose species.

36
00:02:55.103 --> 00:03:00.303
In 2009, Hautier, Niklaus, and Hector added light to their understory.

37
00:03:01.463 --> 00:03:04.883
That prevented the loss, pointing to competition for light.

38
00:03:05.967 --> 00:03:12.887
In 1997, Andrew Beckerman, Maria Uriarte, and Oswald Schmitz tested grasshoppers in

39
00:03:12.887 --> 00:03:14.027
a Connecticut old field.

40
00:03:15.387 --> 00:03:20.527
They compared enclosures with no spiders, hunting spiders, or spiders with glued

41
00:03:20.527 --> 00:03:22.047
mouthparts that could not kill.

42
00:03:23.407 --> 00:03:27.147
Any effect of glued spiders could only come from fear, not killing.

43
00:03:28.447 --> 00:03:33.987
By changing one factor at random beside matched controls, field manipulations turn

44
00:03:33.987 --> 00:03:36.347
tangled patterns into testable causes.
